# The Datalab site's fonts (ADR 0008 "M16 fonts"; legal review 1.9, fix F8). Fetched 2026-10-22
# from the projects' GitHub releases, each an exact tag published long before (> 2 weeks).
#
# Martian Mono v1.1.0 (release published 2025-02-10), SIL OFL 1.1, no Reserved Font Name:
#   https://github.com/evilmartians/mono/releases/download/v1.1.0/martian-mono-1.1.0-variable.zip
#   sha256 b87730975931dc2dbf0129ecf392ccaf8d29f46bc05e995703da4155db510867 (zip)
#   sha256 60e0eee102be3f96b3c2c6431e6bb7101ff20735baee480e091af1765d7d49c7 (MartianMonoVF.ttf in it)
#   The release ships no static 600 (SemiBold), so both weights are instances of the variable
#   font at the Standard width (wdth 100: usWidthClass 5, advance 700, the width the approved
#   spike was rendered at, `font-stretch: 100%`) and wght 400 / 600. The instancer's
#   --update-name-table cannot be used (the font's STAT table has no wght 600 value: "Cannot find
#   Axis Values {'wght': 600.0}"), so each instance is renamed by the script below before
#   subsetting: name IDs 1/2/4/6 (and 16/17 for SemiBold) set to "Martian Mono" / "Regular" /
#   "Martian Mono <style>" / "MartianMono-<style>", the variable font's STAT table dropped; the
#   copyright (0) and licence (13, 14) records are kept.
#   OFL-MartianMono.txt is the repository's OFL.txt at the same tag:
#   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/evilmartians/mono/v1.1.0/OFL.txt
#
# Public Sans v2.001 (release published 2022-05-11), SIL OFL 1.1, no Reserved Font Name:
#   https://github.com/uswds/public-sans/releases/download/v2.001/public-sans-v2.001.zip
#   sha256 88cacdf7cd03b31af8f1f83e1f51e0eb5a6052565a6c014c90c385f1ff2d13a5 (zip)
#   sha256 f3931c3c3ec5301043634ac8f39bcfa7b30d29181864f2fd0c3e6796feacc471 (fonts/webfonts/PublicSans-Regular.woff2)
#   sha256 f99ffc265cc790e0f058a9f430a465c88996008327abb0f8561cb713add40d73 (fonts/webfonts/PublicSans-SemiBold.woff2)
#   OFL-PublicSans.txt is OFL.txt from the same zip.
#
